    "Commit": "60d52099eac3823f3e54226ce6af07ac05d58b5a",
    "CommitMsg": "Graph and Designer View: hierarchy, Find, Focus, details, and group terms\n\n- Both views draw rdfs:subClassOf as well as object properties, and only\n  ontology classes (SKOS concepts no longer appear as stray dots).\n- Find a class by name or IRI; Focus shows 1-3 links around a class (kept in\n  the URL); Show all; switches for hierarchy, group terms, unconnected and\n  deprecated classes; zoom buttons and fit; names and arrow labels by zoom.\n- Large ontologies open at the top of the class hierarchy instead of drawing\n  everything. Graph View settles big layouts before drawing; Designer View\n  layers by the hierarchy and wraps rows at 12 classes.\n- A shared details panel (status, Focus here, Open in Explorer, clickable\n  relationships, properties) lists the groups' terms that reference the class,\n  and with \"Group terms\" on those terms are drawn beside each class.\n- Spec and measurements in docs/graph-views.md; Help and README updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
    "Author": "Ron Synakowski \u003cronnie.synakowski@stardog.com\u003e",
    "Committer": "Ron Synakowski \u003cronnie.synakowski@stardog.com\u003e"
  },
